WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.067 line:92%
-Let's talk about the movie.

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:04.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is based
on a dystopian novel,

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:05.105 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
written in 1953,

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:07.240
about firemen who burn books...
-Yes.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...to stop people
from having ideas.

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:10.276 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And is it safe to say

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:12.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is the most fire
you've been around on set?

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:13.680 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-It's a lot of fire.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I've been
in a bunch of movies

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:17.851 line:92%
where, like, things blew up.

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:20.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
when I did "Pearl Harbor,"

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:21.521 line:92%
they basically re-created --

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Famously.
Things famously blew up.

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, a lot of stuff
blew up there.

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:27.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
But this was interesting.
We started --

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:29.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
My first day
of shooting on this,

00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:32.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's a scene
where we go to Montag's home,

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:34.267 size:88% position:44%
which is the character
Michael B. Jordan plays.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:38.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we basically, like,
burn everything in his house.

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:38.738 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We basically --

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:41.207 size:78% position:39%
We were punishing him
for breaking a rule.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:43.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it was
my first day on the set,

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:44.477 line:92%
and they have us in these --

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:49.616
Our fire suits are basically
these airtight wax costumes

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:50.650 line:92%
that don't breathe at all.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:55.422
And we're on a set in a studio,
and we're just all day long

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:58.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
burning things,
shooting fire out of guns,

00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:01.694
little piles
of smoldering things over there,

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:02.862 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
burning curtains.

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:04.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like 10 hours
of just standing there,

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:06.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
wondering, "What is burning?
What are we inhaling?"

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:07.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:10.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"What is this?
How are they doing this?"

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:10.870 line:92%
And at the end of the day,

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just looked
at Michael B. Jordan,

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:14.541
I was like,
"Man, we know how to pick 'em."

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:15.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:18.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"This is a good time."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:20.513 line:92%
And some of the other guys

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:23.883
had these little cooling systems
under their suits,

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:26.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
all these little,
like, tubes and --

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:29.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
that cold water
would run through.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.591 size:84% position:42%
They basically worked
for about five minutes,

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:33.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then it was basically
like you were covered

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:36.029 size:81% position:41%
with little containers
of pee or something.

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:37.030 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.164 size:78% position:39% line:92%
But I never did that.

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:41.734
I just -- I figured my character
was too tough for that.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's fantastic
that you made that choice.

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:44.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I just sweated it out,
yeah.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:47.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Speaking of toughness,
Michael B. Jordan,

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:49.742
an incredibly tough guy --
obviously, "Black Panther,"

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.878 size:84% position:42%
"Creed" -- not somebody
you want to tango with,

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:55.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you do have a fight scene
with him in the film.

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:57.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
How was that,
going up against somebody --

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was kind of ridiculous,
but, uh...

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.254 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:02.922 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughing ]

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:05.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm a scrapper, though.
I mean...

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.292 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:12.599
But he -- Yeah, he's an awesome
physical specimen.

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:14.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
Something happened
in my profession

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:17.604
that I don't quite understand,
because when I started acting,

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:20.140
the main reason I did it
is because I wasn't an athlete.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:20.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:24.878
-I wasn't into sports, and
I didn't like exercising at all.

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:26.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And now it seems like

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:29.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
actors are expected
to be, like, these --

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:32.752
I think they work out more than,
like, professional bodybuilders.

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:33.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:37.557
-And particularly with all the
superhero movies and whatnot,

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:40.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, people --
I mean -- I'm kind of buddies

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Paul Rudd.
We worked together once.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:46.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when he got "Ant-Man,"
he started working out.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:48.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "You got to work out
to play Ant-Man?"

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:49.235 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
"That doesn't even
make any sense."

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:53.072
-Yeah.
-I mean, I know ants are strong.

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:56.876
I've seen him lift, but they're
not -- they're not bulky.

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:57.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:59.312 size:78% position:39%
-They're not ripped.
-Right, there's no --

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:00.113 line:92%
-They don't have a six-pack.

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:01.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You've never
seen abs on an ant.

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:04.484
-Yeah, it's basically
three little pods and some legs.

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:05.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:07.687
If he was doing a workout
to make himself look like

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
three parts,
then you'd understand.

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:10.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that would make sense.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:13.393
Like some sort of, like,
balloon-animal workout...

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:15.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
...where you twist yourself.

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:16.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Get your head
a little bit bigger.

00:03:16.663 --> 00:03:19.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, exactly.
-Super big torso.

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:20.099 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:22.635
And then, these things,
whatever these are, yeah.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:24.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Almost impossible
to get these at the gym.

00:03:24.771 --> 00:03:28.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-Almost no known workout.

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:29.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no.
-You guys met --

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:33.913
Is it true you met Paul doing
a show together on Broadway?

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:34.781 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-I'd -- I'd known --

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:37.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd been acquainted
with Paul over the years,

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:38.685 line:92%
we had mutual friends in common,

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:41.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we really
got to know one another

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:44.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
doing a play on Broadway,
called "Grace,"

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:51.664
which infamously
was the scene of a vomit that --

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:53.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
a vomiting incident --
-From onstage?

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:54.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In the audience.
-The audience, yeah.

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:58.404 size:81% position:41%
-No, in the audience.
Someone in the balcony

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:00.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
vomited into...
[ Audience groans ]

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:01.441 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
...the orchestra.

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:03.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, so they vomited
all the way down a level?

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:06.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, they vomited --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:08.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
We -- I didn't know
what was happening.

00:04:08.548 --> 00:04:09.282 size:81% position:41% line:92%
We were doing a scene.

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:11.017 size:75% position:38%
There was this scene
in the play where --

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:13.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
where Paul's character
and his wife,

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:16.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
who, ironically,
is now my wife in real life...

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:18.658 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:20.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
-See, that's why
you get into the theater.

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:21.327 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Not to go to the gym.

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:26.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, no, to collect wives.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:27.634 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
No. She --

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:29.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
Somebody had vomited.
So, anyway, there's a scene

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:31.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
where they invite me
over for dinner.

00:04:31.571 --> 00:04:33.673 size:88% position:44%
My character is, like,
this deeply troubled guy

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:36.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
who's been in a car accident,
he's been disfigured,

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:39.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's a scientist --
a physicist --

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:40.513 line:92%
and he's talking about --

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:41.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
they're asking him
about his job,

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:45.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's talking about
the noises that space makes

00:04:45.485 --> 00:04:48.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
and how we get information
from space and --

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:50.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
And while I'm basically
doing this section,

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:54.661
the incident happens
where the vomiting takes place.

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:56.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which I don't hear that,
but what you hear is

00:04:56.663 --> 00:05:01.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
the response to the vomiting,
which is distracting.

00:05:01.768 --> 00:05:02.335 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:06.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I gradually start
to get a little irritated,

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:07.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think,
"Well, isn't this perfect?

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:13.079
I'm actually doing a speech
about how there's noise in space

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:14.380 line:92%
and that it interferes with --

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:19.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I start directly addressing
my speech to the audience

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:21.120 line:92%
in a very a pointed manner

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
and forget
all about Paul and Kate.

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:25.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's basically a scene
between me and the audience

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:29.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
where I'm talking about
noisy, black voids.

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:30.396 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:33.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it just -- it doesn't seem
to be having any effect.

00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:35.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I walk offstage,
I walk past the stage manager,

00:05:35.535 --> 00:05:36.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said,
"What the hell's going on?"

00:05:36.803 --> 00:05:39.605
And he said, "Oh, somebody
just puked in the balcony."

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:42.208 size:75% position:38%
And I immediately --
I felt really bad...

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:42.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:44.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
-'Cause I felt like
I was being very judgmental.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:48.014
I don't know how I would've
handled that situation, really,

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:50.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
if somebody vomited on me.
-Yeah.

00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:51.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel bad for all parties.
-Yeah.

00:05:51.818 --> 00:05:54.420
-You feel bad for --
I feel like the guy who vomited,

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
that wasn't his plan.
-Yeah.

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:59.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, no, I think it was
a foodborne illness.

00:05:59.726 --> 00:06:01.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah?
-Yeah.

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:02.595 line:92%
Although there was speculation

00:06:02.595 --> 00:06:04.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
the person
might have been intoxicated.

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:05.365 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Oh, then, that's --

00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:09.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which I'm not particularly
up on people showing up drunk.

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:12.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it seems
like somebody misunderstands

00:06:12.405 --> 00:06:13.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
the joys of alcohol
if they think,

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:16.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Let's get bombed
and go see a drama."

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:17.377 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:17.377 --> 00:06:19.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, and you got to be
careful, 'cause in that play,

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:22.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
the stage very slowly
spun around the whole time.

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:23.783 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Oh, that's a nightmare.

00:06:23.783 --> 00:06:26.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So if you're drunk and you're
trying to focus, it's --

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:29.555
-Well, if he puked, that's
definitely what the reason was.

00:06:29.555 --> 00:06:32.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I guess it goes
to the old phrase

00:06:32.058 --> 00:06:34.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Turn around's fair play."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:35.795 line:92%
-Well, we'll leave it at that.

00:06:35.795 --> 00:06:38.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being here.

